ng information below:\n\nThe governing differential equation is {{field-1}}.\n\nFor this BVP, the {{field-2}} boundary conditions are {{field-3}}.\n\nThe boundary value problem is {{field-4}}."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "532a73e6-e026-57c9-9bad-57cd2f75b6df" :knowledge-point/title "Parity Recognition and Series Type"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "947d580e-e324-5529-9683-e8139e719d3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228538} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d9c53e-1e0f-5d79-bc2d-834d472fd230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228539}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ce2e7bc3-7f15-5353-86d3-cb49ec8bafbf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a817cf48-1e5e-5542-be82-867759b96aaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228541} {:answer/id #uuid "d02129f7-8b38-5dc9-b416-ed7585af4221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228542}] :answer-field/id #uuid "44a32284-231f-51a0-a7ec-6a638eb11373" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228540}] :question/id #uuid "d7903a61-d4e3-5a7b-991a-79f6efafb8b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-338682" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x) = x\\cos (x)$ on $x ∈ [- π, π]$. Select the correct options below.\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\nConsequently, the\n{{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "472cbb79-e22b-50d2-a997-93130ff66c22" :knowledge-point/title "Trigonometric Eigenfunctions"}] :question/answer-fields [{