n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=6+7=13.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eae6b5d-adff-53b2-970d-f0dcee58365f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems Using Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d068832-722c-5272-8b55-63c50bc79b6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{(s-5)(s+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391805} {:answer/id #uuid "78dc34f1-4b41-5271-9a67-1e6ea193021e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{(s-3)(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391806} {:answer/id #uuid "24eae147-27c5-5438-9f6f-8fdc7f4143dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{(s-3)(s+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391807} {:answer/id #uuid "28fcebc3-7bbd-5a83-82b2-be56dddc1f4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(s-9)(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391808} {:answer/id #uuid "841fa109-b0db-545b-8ff4-ca90114719c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(s-3)(s+9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78dc34f1-4b41-5271-9a67-1e6ea193021e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{(s-3)(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391806} :answer-field/id #uuid "430bf788-0cf9-5d7a-9a1b-c0295a906a26" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391804} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac03c98e-c20c-5d21-a0f8-6f2003603fc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4(s-3)}-\\frac{9}{4(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391811} {:answer/id #uuid "d9323d05-d4e3-56b5-a8da-656c99d133ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{4(s-3)}+\\frac{9}{4(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391812} {:answer/id #uuid "123f5786-dd4b-518f-9769-aa4880fe4b74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8(s-3)}-\\frac{9}{8(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391813} {:answer/id #uuid "5d791733-835d-555a-a11d-7d5c2cc66af0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{8(s-3)}+\\frac{9}{8(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "123f5786-dd4b-518f-9769-aa4880fe4b74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8(s-3)}-\\frac{9}{8(s+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391813} :answer-field/id #uuid "6447376a-9ee8-55d3-b585-57117a2aa52b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391810} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3be51800-b0ed-50eb-baf5-dad262e05f23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391816} {:answer/id #uuid "9841a98c-71dd-5259-9345-a25d81d7cccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{3t}+\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391817} {:answer/id #uuid "4c606eb4-f1b8-514d-a32c-b40fac8b4d65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-3t}+\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391818} {:answer/id #uuid "ec303ae8-3dca-5c9e-a783-c40d551cc915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-3t}-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3be51800-b0ed-50eb-baf5-dad262e05f23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391816} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bc41c25-e0a5-593e-84b7-fb349ac21dde" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31e8084f-ab1a-5236-ac36-9b6a9937b2ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-342499" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+5y=9{e}^{3t},\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms.\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+5L{y}=L{9{e}^{3t}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative, $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0),$ and the standard transform \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\,s>a,\n$$\n\n \nwe substitute the known values.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sY(s)-0+5Y(s) & =9\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-3} \\\\ (s+5)Y(s) & =\\frac{9}{s-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $Y(s),$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{9}{(s-3)(s+5)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. We write $Y(s)$ in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{(s-3)(s+5)}=\\frac{A}{s-3}+\\frac{B}{s+5}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants $A$ and $B,$ we first clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n9=A(s+5)+B(s-3)\n$$\n\nNow, we find the constants $A$ and $B.$\n\n- Setting $s=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n9=A(3+5)+B(0)\\,⟹\\,9=8A\\,⟹\\,A=\\frac{9}{8}.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-5,$ we have\n\n$$\n9=A(0)+B(-5-3)\\,⟹\\,9=-8B\\,⟹\\,B=-\\frac{9}{8}.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{9}{8(s-3)}-\\frac{9}{8(s+5)}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-3}} & ={e}^{3t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+5}} & ={e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =\\frac{9}{8}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-3}}-\\frac{9}{8}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+5}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{9}{8}{e}^{-5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167301 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3cb7656-1ce6-5b6a-9e88-5ba24a943c3f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Infinite Sum Using Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "088118d9-d82e-5555-ae2d-6b6c94d1c0ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1)^{n+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391821} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc13dfa-2ecd-5239-9fbb-48bd4bb71145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391822} {:answer/id #uuid "7f1eb88d-b598-57b0-9201-7890985133cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391823} {:answer/id #uuid "1eddfbd5-9f38-5c59-b2d4-5ed1bfea29b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1)^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dc13dfa-2ecd-5239-9fbb-48bd4bb71145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391822} :answer-field/id #uuid "74dce7e8-8cd9-587e-b02b-722f57c4a1c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5fa43ec-082f-5051-8bd2-f2697aaabdbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391826} {:answer/id #uuid "d1477410-5650-553a-8e7e-4f722e3de5c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391827} {:answer/id #uuid "86d236a1-c815-5c11-9ff9-24c7f3e6f09e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391828} {:answer/id #uuid "304ead85-1477-5158-9c81-f158cc755a50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5fa43ec-082f-5051-8bd2-f2697aaabdbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391826} :answer-field/id #uuid "e80d872f-e8aa-5257-8cb5-be49497a6b44" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391825} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3721b96f-c770-5ed4-b0bb-886380288864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391831} {:answer/id #uuid "3ee6cd9d-926e-5f7e-80f3-b512fbbfd9a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391832} {:answer/id #uuid "6242ee14-aa46-52e1-9ea4-3919fdb9fd79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6242ee14-aa46-52e1-9ea4-3919fdb9fd79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391833} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9e3c3e8-cafb-59da-905f-3dfdbc9e7c24" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391830} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5889a416-25b2-5826-9187-131a2ada5c3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391835} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f8e8b6-6e4f-5f2a-a120-02c5bf806f42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "discontinuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5889a416-25b2-5826-9187-131a2ada5c3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391835} :answer-field/id #uuid "50452121-b236-57c2-988c-53f0a2c87054" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f28129a8-5e3e-5ca3-8128-6017fbcdb672" :question/math-academy-id "q-342573" :question/problem "Consider the function $F(x)=|x|$ defined on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ The Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{\\pi }{2}-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{\\pi (2n-1)^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.At $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)\\cdot 0)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(0)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}={{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)\\cdot 0)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(0)=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡((2n-1)\\cdot 0) \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot 1 \\\\ -\\frac{\\pi }{2} & =-\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}} & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eae6b5d-adff-53b2-970d-f0dcee58365f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems Using Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "682c0743-ced4-575b-9b11-bb0ed2397471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391839} {:answer/id #uuid "e24cb923-a73f-5f55-8cc4-7366a46db4f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391840} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d7e4a0-8878-50a2-82bf-c36c22547d09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391841} {:answer/id #uuid "a92f4310-7745-5554-be5b-d2c37d364da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a92f4310-7745-5554-be5b-d2c37d364da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391842} :answer-field/id #uuid "66a35915-30b2-56a9-9216-501c50a79a6a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391838} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2234c02c-40c5-5fe8-9294-8f978b3b33f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+2t-2{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391844} {:answer/id #uuid "eb715303-088e-59da-887a-dc46d69a5b33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2-2t+2{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391845} {:answer/id #uuid "a0987410-57a3-5132-b4c5-a1fa4e946c3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2+2t+2{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391846} {:answer/id #uuid "9b141dfa-42d6-5e24-b4e3-cd06abaa43ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-2t-2{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2234c02c-40c5-5fe8-9294-8f978b3b33f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+2t-2{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391844} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9238576-38b0-5b50-b1bb-1b1d795ebe7a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391843} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2297b2a9-99f1-5d35-98cd-9f8bc170f8c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391849} {:answer/id #uuid "3106c57f-a902-5ed6-b068-5c13cfa8c306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4s-2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391850} {:answer/id #uuid "d9669eb7-a297-526c-bab3-5121152922d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2s+4}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391851} {:answer/id #uuid "512e45ed-4107-5534-b3ef-0d4173824d42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4s+2}{s(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391852} {:answer/id #uuid "1cba4342-4e1f-5a64-a4de-dd0fde359471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2297b2a9-99f1-5d35-98cd-9f8bc170f8c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391849} :answer-field/id #uuid "3969cc27-8978-59e6-a3a9-64eb91b6fb2e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d4a5a1a-5811-5a7d-99a0-f3fb86ea4705" :question/math-academy-id "q-342704" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y=2t+4,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},\\,s>0,\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+L{y}=2L{t}+4L{1}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard polynomial transforms\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{t} & =\\frac{1!}{{s}^{1+1}}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}, \\\\ L{1} & =\\frac{0!}{{s}^{0+1}}=\\frac{1}{s},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-0)+Y(s) & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{4}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{4s}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+1)$ and a repeated linear factor ${s}^{2},$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}=\\frac{A}{s}+\\frac{B}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n4s+2=As(s+1)+B(s+1)+C{s}^{2}\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-1,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n4(-1)+2=A(0)+B(0)+C(-1)^{2}\\,⟹\\,-2=C\\,⟹\\,C=-2.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=0,$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n4(0)+2=A(0)+B(0+1)+C(0)\\,⟹\\,2=B\\,⟹\\,B=2.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of $s,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n4=A+B\\,⟹\\,4=A+2\\,⟹\\,A=2.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} & =1 \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}} & =t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} & ={e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}}-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} \\\\ y(t) & =2+2t-2{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06fedec8-5aed-52f9-bd4f-aa81b9180ad4" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems With Sinusoidal Forcing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b2fb4b0-07f3-5625-9c49-65c3c22c214d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s+1}-\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391856} {:answer/id #uuid "10170df4-7484-54f0-aa33-015457180f80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391857} {:answer/id #uuid "1ca6fa42-9c37-510f-83a3-98293a7e6dac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391858} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa88e62-d2a3-55c8-8a49-8f813370fc06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8aa88e62-d2a3-55c8-8a49-8f813370fc06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391859} :answer-field/id #uuid "d464ce20-0af7-533c-95b4-ac51b5fb72d7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391855} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "639d737a-dc43-5b5e-af1d-e0afd225199a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{2}+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391861} {:answer/id #uuid "1b9316f6-9bda-5687-bc9b-530c9452e5d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+2}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391862} {:answer/id #uuid "4d2e0173-d30c-5202-8012-80c2996c781b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391863} {:answer/id #uuid "cb79fe15-e7d0-52f8-870d-d8f97b03e48e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391864} {:answer/id #uuid "79f3838d-b1f0-5ab6-a84c-06bc3e4b1800" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{s}^{2}+s+2}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d2e0173-d30c-5202-8012-80c2996c781b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391863} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3ad48e6-1c4a-5293-b3ab-2d2d527d6e6e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de9a3b40-9a85-5539-aeb6-2bae92e01638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391867} {:answer/id #uuid "76e6cb33-fd81-56d8-b7aa-8b5868954f20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-t}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391868} {:answer/id #uuid "d048494a-db77-5c1a-99ed-d7081b6cfd92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391869} {:answer/id #uuid "e88ce333-a1ba-58d1-8a93-e33206d5ca72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e88ce333-a1ba-58d1-8a93-e33206d5ca72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391870} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eff5f4a-7b85-50da-b6a0-8e1674f2078e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f44dbcab-4002-5eb8-9303-ab06ab01d7f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-343057" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following results:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+L{y}=L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-2)+Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s)-2 & =\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, add $2$ to the right-hand side and find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+1)Y(s) & =2+\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}+1)}{{s}^{2}+1}+\\frac{s+1}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+1)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+1),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{s}^{2}+s+3}{(s+1)({s}^{2}+1)}=\\frac{A}{s+1}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n2{s}^{2}+s+3=A({s}^{2}+1)+(Bs+C)(s+1)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-1,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n2(-1)^{2}+(-1)+3=A((-1)^{2}+1)+0\\,⟹\\,4=2A\\,⟹\\,A=2.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n2=A+B\\,⟹\\,2=2+B\\,⟹\\,B=0.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n3=A+C\\,⟹\\,3=2+C\\,⟹\\,C=1.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} & ={e}^{-t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}} \\\\ y(t) & =2{e}^{-t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49a83d03-bcec-5b15-ad52-b1e7c32edc9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391872} {:answer/id #uuid "880e8c11-d342-5705-af1b-e6abf47c5224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391873} {:answer/id #uuid "0fbbdb7c-314c-5954-a1ec-3f2ec80b9ff4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391874} {:answer/id #uuid "0eee38af-d79e-5905-9c03-fc841d170da3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391875} {:answer/id #uuid "919f5be6-a5f1-5fa3-a69f-295d49529851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "919f5be6-a5f1-5fa3-a69f-295d49529851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391876} :answer-field/id #uuid "46545e04-c37a-551e-b919-1faa52207c4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dcd84fb5-e504-5016-bbba-4d8edb437f6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-34333" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{2}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=-2{x}_{2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391877 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f0198d9-f83e-5d0e-a8f2-b00c3ca2d46b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391879} {:answer/id #uuid "5f0421dd-4b76-5b27-941c-50a51355f127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391880} {:answer/id #uuid "98535724-16db-586b-94d6-47675062a82b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391881} {:answer/id #uuid "fb7b7c44-935c-5b9c-95d9-ab7dff1476d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391882} {:answer/id #uuid "4d601e9e-c427-56eb-9ac5-b71bffd8d3e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ -11{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb7b7c44-935c-5b9c-95d9-ab7dff1476d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391882} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fde154e-f5aa-5ee6-91b0-0f999f1f1a17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d54de9d5-0eaf-51ac-a971-a5633a39368a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34334" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, and we have one free variables, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}.$ Substituting ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}$ into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(4{x}_{3})+3{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-11{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$"}]}
